{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HJR001","billNumberShort":"H.J.R. 1","billNumberLong":"HJR001S04","fileNumber":"2026FL0813","shortTitle":"Joint Rules Resolution - Amendments to Joint Rules","currentSubVersion":"4","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"DUNNIJA","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Dunnigan, James A.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"FILLML","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Fillmore, Lincoln","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This resolution modifies joint rules.","highlightedProvisions":"This resolution:<hr><ltbullet>defines \"minority leader\" and \"minority party\";<hr><ltbullet>modifies the definition of \"increase legislative workload\";<hr><ltbullet>clarifies the secretary of the Senate's and the chief clerk of the House's record keeping duties;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the publication of the Senate and House draft journals;<hr><ltbullet>addresses rules and procedures that apply to an extraordinary session;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes the Office of Legislative Research and General Counsel to request a bill on behalf of a legislator if the bill is necessary to implement a constitutional joint resolution; <hr><ltbullet>allows a legislator to co-sponsor legislation that originates in the opposite chamber of which the legislator is a member;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies provisions related to committee notes;<hr><ltbullet>defines \"sunset bill\" and requires:<hr><ltbullet1>the Senate to table a House sunset bill on third reading; and<hr><ltbullet1>the House to refer a Senate sunset bill to the House Rules Committee; <hr><ltbullet>modifies the process related to legislation that increases legislative workload; <hr><ltbullet>modifies a Legislative Expenses Oversight Committee's meeting requirements; <hr><ltbullet>limits the number of committee bill files that an authorized legislative committee may open; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Megan L. Bolin","fis